{title: Harbor Lights}
{subtitle: An original test song for Strudelizer (ChordPro format)}
{key: G}
{tempo: 92}
{x_pickup: 2}
# Every Decision 2 spelling appears below. Two lines must be reported as
# unparsed: the one with [Q7] and the unknown {flourish} directive.

{start_of_verse}
[D]Out on the [G]water the [Gmaj7]evening comes [Em7]slow
[Cadd9]Lanterns are [D]swinging, [G/B]two by [C]two
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[Em]Harbor [Bm7]lights, [CM7]carry me [D7]home
[G6]Over the [Em9]tide where the [Am7]old ships [D]roam
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Emin]Ropes on the [Am6]pier and the [Bdim]gulls in the [B7]air
[E-]Salt on the [C^7]window, [CΔ]light in your [Asus2]hair
[Dsus4]Bells from the [D°]church as the [F#m7b5]wind turns [B+]cold
[Bø]Stories the [Baug]sailors have [Cm]told
[D9]Lights [Q7]fading [G]out
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge}
[Cm]Hold the [Gm]line, [Am]hold the [D]line
{end_of_bridge}
{flourish: big}
[G]
